our DevOps group.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.000
And similarly, something
similar for the Linux VMs.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:46.130
Maybe it's some other
group or maybe it's DevOps.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:49.380
And similarly for the cloud
storage access policy.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:53.180
So when you set these up, what
that means is that obviously

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:57.117
locking down in a very
big way, you can't--

00:07:57.117 --> 00:07:59.450
for example, I could be logged
in as some Gmail account.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.007
And I can't access this anymore.

00:08:01.007 --> 00:08:03.090
And however, at this point,
I'll just make a point

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.510
that somebody in
the DevOps group

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.360
can maintain that App Engine
or change the settings, IAM

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.310
settings or whatever it
might be, or use APIs

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:11.530
against against App Engine.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.472
They could do it
